 ## Overview
-A CPU-side controller for interactive voxel painting and erasing that determines the brush position and surface normal on a voxel grid via DDA raycasting, with a fallback to ray-AABB intersection when voxel data is unavailable [S1, unofficial]. It differs from global noise generation by allowing localized, immediate edits via mouse input, bridging the gap between static voxel generation and dynamic user interaction [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Voxel selection via pick ray intersection](893-voxel-selection-via-pick-ray-intersection.md) by implementing the specific raycasting logic for voxel selection [S1, unofficial].
+A CPU-side controller for interactive voxel painting and erasing that determines the brush position and surface normal on a voxel grid using Digital Differential Analysis (DDA) raycasting [S1, unofficial]. It differs from its parent [Voxel selection via pick ray intersection](893-voxel-selection-via-pick-ray-intersection.md) by providing the specific state management and fallback logic for direct manipulation, and from siblings like [Reverse Index Map for Voxel Location](1097-reverse-index-map-for-voxel-location.md) by relying on traversal rather than lookup tables [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-- **Inputs:** Mouse screen coordinates in normalized device coordinates (NDC), camera state (position, forward, right, up vectors, field of view, aspect ratio), voxel grid data, and brush parameters (radius, material, mode, shape) [S1, unofficial].
-- **Outputs:** Updated `m_brushPosition` in world space, updated voxel grid state after painting or erasing, and hit voxel coordinates with surface normal for rendering feedback [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Inputs:** Camera position (`cameraPos`), camera basis vectors (`cameraForward`, `cameraRight`, `cameraUp`), field of view (`fov`), aspect ratio, mouse NDC coordinates (`mouseNDC.x`, `mouseNDC.y`), mouse button states (`leftButtonDown`, `rightButtonDown`), scroll delta (`scrollDelta`), voxel grid data (`voxelGridData`), grid size (`voxelGridSize`), and grid bounds (`m_gridMin`, `m_gridMax`).
+*   **Outputs:** Updated brush state (`m_brushPosition`, `m_radius`, `m_material`, `m_mode`, `m_shape`), and a hit result indicating whether a voxel was found.
 
